### Keyset paging over a NULLABLE sort key, which was refused outright before F4 — and refused for a
### reason: the boundary was a chain of comparisons with no `IS NULL` arm, so paging over such a key
### silently dropped rows. `scheduled_for` is set on two of the seven seeded work orders and null on
### five, so both a null-keyed anchor and a valued one occur in every walk below.
###
### `nullslast` first: the null-keyed tail is what used to be unreachable, because every comparison
### against a NULL is NULL and a WHERE treats that as false.
# @name LastPage1
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&order=scheduled_for.asc.nullslast
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name LastPage2
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&order=scheduled_for.asc.nullslast&after={{LastPage1.response.body.$.next}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name LastPage3
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&order=scheduled_for.asc.nullslast&after={{LastPage2.response.body.$.next}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name LastPage4
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=2&order=scheduled_for.asc.nullslast&after={{LastPage3.response.body.$.next}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The whole set in one request, so the walk is compared with the truth rather than with itself
# @name LastWholeSet
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=100&order=scheduled_for.asc.nullslast
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `nullsfirst` is the sharper case: page one's anchor is itself a null-keyed row, which is the shape
### that used to make page two come back empty.
